    "created_at": "2023-03-16T13:42:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-03-16T13:42:03Z",
    "body": "My thinking about it is to use have a \"fake\" request with `prefetch` initiator and perform a CSP check on that (with the newly defined CSP rules for prefetch).\r\n\r\nWe can wrap connect+resolve in Fetch with a call that accepts a client instead of partition key that makes this call.\r\n\r\nbtw a very different alternative I thought about is to have a \"preconnect\" or \"dns-prefetch\" destination, and exit early inside fetch based on that destination. WDYT @annevk ?\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
